---
source: crates/kagebunshin/src/cli/mod.rs
expression: sub.clone().render_help().to_string()
---
Create projects and add environments and sources, without editing TOML

Usage: kagebunshin project [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init           Create a project, identified by its git remotes, with one environment
  remove         Remove a project: delete its file
  add-env        Add an environment to a project
  add-source     Add a source to an environment; a later source wins over an earlier one
  remove-source  Remove one of an environment's sources
  move-source    Move one of an environment's sources, changing which wins a key two set
  dedupe         Remove an environment's exact duplicate sources, keeping the copy that wins
  set-source     Change the AWS profile or region of an environment's aws_sm sources
  set-var        Set a plain setting of an environment, one that is not secret (PORT=3000)
  unset-var      Remove a plain setting of an environment
  set            Change a project's AWS profile, or with --env an environment's
  list           List the projects, each with its folder, environments and providers
  show           Print a project's configuration: names and settings, never values
  facts          Print what this checkout and the connected providers say, names only
  example        Write the app's .env.example from the keys its code reads, names only
  apply          Check a project file in a dry run, then install it, all or nothing
  draft          Draft a project file for this checkout from what it and the providers say
  help           Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json            Print machine-readable JSON; errors go to stderr as JSON
      --socket <PATH>   Daemon socket [default: $KAGEBUNSHIN_SOCKET, else a per-user runtime dir]
      --env <ENV>       Environment to use instead of the project's default
      --project <NAME>  Project to use instead of the one for this folder; it must claim this checkout's remotes
  -h, --help            Print help
  -V, --version         Print version
